  "question": {
    "text": "A point source of heat of power <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> is placed at the centre of a thin spherical shell of mean radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>. The material of the shell has thermal conductivity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi></math>. Calculate the thickness&nbsp;of the shell if the temperature difference between the outer and inner surfaces of the shell in steady-state is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi></math>.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
