  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Consider a concentric spherical shell of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math>&nbsp;and thickness <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>r</mi></math> as shown in diagram. The radial rate of flow of heat through this shell in steady state will be,<br /><br /><strong><u><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/EM0013992_AnsExp3_1.jpg\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 197px;\" /></u></strong><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">H</mtext><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mtext>d</mtext><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">Q</mtext></mrow><mrow><mtext>d</mtext><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">t</mtext></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">KA</mtext><mfrac><mrow><mtext>d</mtext><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">&#952;</mtext></mrow><mrow><mtext>d</mtext><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">r</mtext></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br />[Negative sign is used because, with an increase in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi></math>&nbsp;decreases.]<br /><br />Now as for spherical shell <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math><br /><br />So<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mspace width=\"0.5em\"/><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">H</mtext><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mtext>&#960;</mtext><msup><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">r</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">K</mtext><mfrac><mrow><mtext>d</mtext><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">&#952;</mtext></mrow><mrow><mtext>d</mtext><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">r</mtext></mrow></mfrac><mspace width=\"0.5em\"/><mspace width=\"0.5em\"/><mtext>or</mtext><mspace width=\"0.5em\"/><mspace width=\"0.5em\"/><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mfrac><mrow><mtext>d</mtext><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">r</mtext></mrow><msup><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">r</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mtext>&#960;</mtext><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">K</mtext></mrow><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">H</mtext></mfrac><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><msub><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">&#952;</mtext><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">&#952;</mtext><mn>2</mn></msub></msubsup><mtext>d</mtext><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">&#952;</mtext></math><br /><br />which on integration and simplification gives<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">H</mtext><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mtext>d</mtext><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">Q</mtext></mrow><mrow><mtext>d</mtext><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">t</mtext></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">K</mtext><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mtext>&#960;</mtext><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mfenced><mrow><msub><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">&#952;</mtext><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">&#952;</mtext><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mfenced><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced></mfrac><mspace width=\"0.5em\"/><mspace width=\"0.5em\"/><mspace width=\"0.5em\"/><mspace width=\"0.5em\"/><mspace width=\"0.5em\"/><mspace width=\"0.5em\"/><mspace width=\"0.5em\"/><mspace width=\"0.5em\"/><mspace width=\"0.5em\"/><mspace width=\"0.5em\"/><mtext>...(i)</mtext></math><br /><br />Now in steady state, as no heat is absorbed, the rate of loss of heat by conduction is equal to that of supply, i.e., <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>H</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>P</mi></math>, and here<br /><br />&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></math> &nbsp; and &nbsp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">a</mtext><mo>&#8771;</mo><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">b</mtext><mo>=</mo><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">R</mtext></math><br /><br />So Equation (i) becomes,<br /><br />&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">P</mtext><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">R</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">KT</mtext></mrow><mfenced><mrow><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">b</mtext><mo>-</mo><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">a</mtext></mrow></mfenced></mfrac></math><br /><br />i.e thickness of shell is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">R</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">KT</mtext></mrow><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">P</mtext></mfrac></math>",
    "image": null
  },
